  "sampling": "One representative per codec/container group, not all1328 files. Input codec/container/rate come from actual server MediaStreams/MediaSources metadata. Source metadata/durations are unaltered. MP4-family is the server-reported format string, not a claim that each extension was tested.",
  "method": [
    "Copy the already-authorized isolated protected connection/device identity into disposable app data. Read only the named authorized Jellyfin origin; block all non-GET/HEAD and nonlocal-provider origins. Do not sign in again or mutate the server.",
    "The fixture reports502 for direct media attempts only, routing the actual production one-time fallback into the server universal endpoint. The conversion response, codec request, time offset, bytes and native decoding are real; no fake audio/metadata/duration is supplied. This does not claim these sources naturally fail direct decoding.",
    "The production unbuffered response passes through a TransformStream that forwards every byte unchanged and retains only the first128KiB for codec inspection. It does not add Content-Length or buffer the whole recording.",
    "Native CUA Command-R installs a passive Audio-constructor observer before React creates its actual media elements. The observer retains actual instances without replacing media methods or duration getters. All Play/Pause/Next/Tab/PageUp/PageDown input is native CUA. Playwright is launch/read-only telemetry only.",
    "For each representative: start converted playback and observe actual native media progress, pause and keyboard-seek forward, then resume and keyboard-seek backward. Actual server startTimeTicks matches the requested offset. Paused seeks stay paused; playing seeks continue decoding and advancing. The finite catalog duration keeps the slider usable despite native progressive duration Infinity.",
    "ffprobe independently parses the sampled real output bytes as MP3 for every playback/seek offset. No media bytes, song titles, item IDs, tokens or credential files are committed."
  ],
